So, just to confirm, I ran 'mt -f /dev/sa0 erase' and I received a I/O
error. Unless I am doing something wrong, it seems to me that 'mt' may have
an issue. Be it either that it is broken, or it doesn't like my tape drive
and dump does.

I do have a TZ89 DLT drive that I can try as well, if anyone thinks that is
needed.

